module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Topology.PiSixSphereThreeWanted
namespace Topology.PiSixSphereThree

/-!
# The sixth homotopy group of the 3-sphere

`π₆(𝕊³) ≅ ℤ/12`, as tabulated by Toda. This is the earliest homotopy group of
a sphere to have composite order (shared with the isomorphic `π₆(𝕊²)`): the
2-primary component `ℤ/4` is generated by Toda's `ν'`, and the 3-primary
component `ℤ/3` by the first odd-primary alpha element `α₁(3)`.

The statement follows the explicit-basepoint conventions of
`LeanEval.Topology.HomotopyGroups`.
-/

/- **π₆ of the 3-sphere.** Toda's tables give `π₆(𝕊³) ≅ ℤ/12`. -/
/-- **The sixth homotopy group of the 3-sphere.** Let $S^3$ be the unit sphere in Euclidean space
$\mathbb{R}^4$. For every point $x \in S^3$, the homotopy group $\pi_6(S^3, x)$ is isomorphic as a
group to the cyclic group $\mathbb{Z}/12$.

Source: H. Toda, 'Composition Methods in Homotopy Groups of Spheres', Annals of Mathematics Studies 49, Princeton University Press, 1962. The value pi_6(S^3) = Z/12 also appears in the tables of A. Hatcher, 'Algebraic Topology', Section 4.1. Via leanprover/lean-eval@38361be, problem `pi6_sphere_three_mulEquiv_zmod_twelve`. -/
public theorem_wanted pi6_sphere_three_mulEquiv_zmod_twelve
    (x : Metric.sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)) 1) :
    Nonempty
      (HomotopyGroup.Pi 6 (Metric.sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)) 1) x ≃*
        Multiplicative (ZMod 12))

end Topology.PiSixSphereThree

end MathlibExt.Topology.PiSixSphereThreeWanted
